1
00:02:05,703 --> 00:02:06,466
<v Liz>Hello?


2
00:02:06,466 --> 00:02:09,067
<v Ken> Hi Liz, it’s Ken here.


3
00:02:09,067 --> 00:02:12,632
<v Liz>Hi Ken! Nice to hear from you! Are you ...


4
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:28,383
<v Ken>This is just a quick call, but Mary and I have just been talking about our summer holiday - we haven’t booked a place yet and we’ve left it a bit late. We were just wondering if you know of any holiday rentals in your area - it’s so nice there.


5
00:02:28,383 --> 00:02:35,230
<v Liz>Well yes, I can think of two or three places that are very nice - what dates have you got in mind?


6
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:38,395
<v Ken>Example The 10th of July to the 22nd of July.


7
00:02:38,395 --> 00:02:45,886
<v Liz> Oh yes, that is quite soon isn’t it? Well there’s a place near here called  Moonfleet ...


8
00:02:45,876 --> 00:02:50,040
<v Ken> Is that M-double O- N-F-L-double E- T?


9
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:59,819
<v Liz> That’s right. It’s quite a rural location, and it’s next to the owner’s house, but it’s got fields all around it, so it’s very pretty.


10
00:02:59,809 --> 00:03:04,146
<v Ken> Mm. Sounds OK. Can you tell me a bit more about it?


11
00:03:04,146 --> 00:03:12,771
<v Liz>Well it’s an annexe to the owner’s house, and it’s an apartment with two bedrooms, and an open-plan living area.


12
00:03:12,771 --> 00:03:17,822
<v Ken> Well I like the sound of it. Is there anything we might not like about it?


13
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:21,719
<v Liz>Well it’s quite a distance from the nearest shops, that’s all ...


14
00:03:21,719 --> 00:03:30,839
<v Ken>OK. And ... well, I’ll tell Mary but I don’t think she’d mind that. Do you know how you book it?


15
00:03:30,839 --> 00:03:38,420
<v Liz>You have to book on the internet. There’s a web address - it’s www. summerhouses ...


16
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:39,375
<v Ken>One word?


17
00:03:39,375 --> 00:03:44,463
<v Liz>Yes ... Then dot com. You’ll be able to look at a photograph on that.


18
00:03:44,463 --> 00:03:47,772
<v Ken>OK . And what about the others? Where are they?


19
00:03:47,772 --> 00:04:02,819
<v Liz>The second one I’m thinking of is called Kingfisher, and that’s even more rural. It’s a really beautiful location in fact, it’s by the Q5 river, and it’s got nice views - it overlooks woodland on the other side.


20
00:04:02,819 --> 00:04:04,699
<v Ken>Is that an apartment?


21
00:04:04,699 --> 00:04:16,948
<v Liz>No, it’s a three-bedroomed house. And that’s got a Q6 dining room as well as a separate living room and a kitchen. But I expect it’s more expensive. You’ll have to check the prices.


22
00:04:16,948 --> 00:04:26,121
<v Ken>Mm. It’s probably a bit bigger than we need, but our nephew might be joining us, we’re not sure yet. How do you book Kingfisher?


23
00:04:26,121 --> 00:04:38,484
<v Liz> You have to phone the owner directly. Shall I give you the number? I’ve got it here in my phone book ... It’s oh one seven five two, double six nine, two one eight.


24
00:04:38,484 --> 00:04:40,112
<v Ken> Right ...


25
00:05:13,402 --> 00:05:14,871
<v Ken>And you mentioned a third place?


26
00:05:14,871 --> 00:05:20,201
<v Liz>Yes, there’s a house that my sister stayed in last year - it’s called Sunnybanks.


27
00:05:20,201 --> 00:05:21,263
<v Ken>Nice name.


28
00:05:21,263 --> 00:05:29,751
<v Liz>And the location of that one is rather different ... It’s in the centre of a village, but it’s a very small and quaint place.


29
00:05:29,751 --> 00:05:31,181
<v Ken>Did your sister like it?


30
00:05:31,181 --> 00:05:36,346
<v Liz>Oh yes, it’s by the sea so her children really loved it ...


31
00:05:36,336 --> 00:05:37,979
<v Ken>What’s the accommodation like?


32
00:05:37,979 --> 00:05:54,416
<v Liz> I’m not sure about the number of rooms because I haven’t been in it myself, but I think she said it’s quite spacious ... And I know it’s got its own garden. It’s not very big, but it’s not shared with anyone else, and it’s supposed to be very pretty.


33
00:05:54,416 --> 00:05:56,312
<v Ken>Any snags? Problems?


34
00:05:56,312 --> 00:06:09,155
<v Liz>The only other thing I can think of is that there’s nowhere for parking. The streets are too narrow. So you have to leave your car somewhere else and then walk to the house - it’s only about ten minutes away, but ...


35
00:06:09,155 --> 00:06:14,871
<v Ken>OK. Well ... I don’t think it matters personally. How do you book it?


36
00:06:14,871 --> 00:06:21,647
<v Liz>There’s an agent you have to contact. I don’t know his details, but I can ask my sister and let you know tomorrow.


37
00:06:21,647 --> 00:06:27,683
<v Ken>Thanks Liz, that’d be great. I’ll talk to Mary and see what she says. Thanks for your help.


38
00:06:27,683 --> 00:06:33,092
<v Liz>That’s OK Ken, I’ll speak to you again tomorrow. I hope you find what you’re looking for ...